{
  "_comment": [
    "Registry of RL policies selectable from the RL web page's dropdown.",
    "Hand-maintained: add an entry when you export a new .onnx into rl_policy/",
    "(or rl_policy/policies/). Fields:",
    "  id             stable key used by the API/UDP link (kebab/underscore, no spaces)",
    "  name           human label shown in the dropdown",
    "  model          checkpoint / training run description (2nd dropdown column)",
    "  type           'blind' (proprioceptive only) or 'camera' (needs a height scan)",
    "  control        'velocity' (default, joystick-driven), 'forward' (joystick-driven",
    "                 but FORWARD-BIASED: the move stick's lateral axis is read as a",
    "                 turn-toward request, not a strafe -- see the stepfield-fwd task)",
    "                 or 'posture' (sit/stand, driven by the RL Actions panel instead",
    "                 of the joystick). Descriptive only: it labels the web joystick.",
    "                 deploy.yaml's commands.base_velocity.style is what the node acts",
    "                 on, and go2_rl_policy_node warns if the two disagree.",
    "  obs_dim        expected observation width; reported if it disagrees with the onnx",
    "  uses_heightmap true if the obs includes the 187-ray height scan",
    "  runnable       false if it cannot run through the current RL launcher at all",
    "                 (e.g. no exported onnx on this robot). NOT a perception flag any",
    "                  more: go2_rl_bridge_node forwards /go2/height_scan across the UDP",
    "                  link, so a uses_heightmap policy CAN run -- provided the perception",
    "                  stack is live. Start it with:",
    "                    ros2 launch go2_bringup real_perception.launch.py rviz:=false",
    "                  (needs the OUTER Go2_RL_workflow workspace built + sourced, for",
    "                   go2_msgs and go2_perception). Whether a scan is actually arriving",
    "                  is decided at engage time by go2_rl_policy_node, which refuses to",
    "                  release the sport service without one newer than 0.4 s and ESTOPs",
    "                  if the scan goes stale mid-run. A static flag cannot know that.",
    "  path           onnx path, relative to rl_policy/ (or absolute)",
    "  group          dropdown section header shown in the in-window panel and HTML",
    "                 <optgroup>. Keep same-group entries consecutive.",
    "The backend also reports a computed 'available' flag (whether the file exists).",
    "",
    "EVERY policy now needs a deploy.yaml BESIDE ITS .onnx. Training writes it from the",
    "live env (training/go2_training/utils/export_deploy_cfg.py); the node reads it for",
    "action scale, kp/kd, control rate, the default pose and the observation layout.",
    "A policy without one is refused, not run on this file's values -- those are",
    "hand-typed, and every one of them fails silently when wrong.",
    "The fields above are now descriptive (they drive the dropdown and are cross-checked",
    "against the contract); deploy.yaml is authoritative."
  ],
